🚀 Implementation Plan: Hybrid Cloud & Offline-First Language App
🛠️ 1. System Architecture & Data Topology
To achieve maximum reliability, affordability, and performance, data is split strategically across services:

A. Online Cloud Layer
Supabase Database (PostgreSQL): Stores user profiles, application core text (words/phrases), and structured payment/financial data.

Supabase Storage (Buckets): Stores user profile avatars and transaction proof images (receipt screenshots).

Cloudflare D1 Database (SQLite): Stores audio file metadata and streaming paths linked to your bucket infrastructure (Database ID: ceba9320-4b75-46b5-8077-d96c4c627176).

B. Local Client Layer (Offline-First Engine)
IndexedDB (via Dexie.js): Aggregates data from both Supabase and Cloudflare D1. It stores text locally as standard rows and caches audio files locally as binary Blobs so the app remains fully functional without an internet connection.

